A Caju é uma empresa brasileira de tecnologia , que busca dar mais sabor à vida profissional, transformando a relação entre empresas e colaboradores por meio de soluções mais inovadoras e seguras como o Cartão Multi Benefícios, Solução em Despesas Corporativas, Premiações e Caju Ciclos.

Aqui na Caju , aprendemos sempre , e nos tornamos cada vez melhores em um ambiente colaborativo e divertido! São muito bem-vindas candidaturas de pessoas negras/pretas, mulheres, indígenas, LGBTQIA+, ou outros grupos minorizados. Inscreva-se e conheça mais sobre nosso time 🧡
Definir as estratégias de produto de pagamentos conectadas com a visão de negócio da Caju ;
Definir os requisitos de produto de pagamentos de acordo com normas técnicas vigentes seja do BACEN, bandeira ou outros;
Definir e validar o roadmap da squad com stakeholders estratégicos e alta liderança;
Definir os indicadores de sucesso do produto e análises relevantes que devem ser feitas para a melhoria contínua;
Tomar decisões de impacto e realizar negociações complexas com stakeholders estratégicos;
Antecipar problemas que podem impactar o prazo;
Compartilhar responsabilidades e expectativas de prazo com pares funcionais e mensurar os impactos de possíveis atrasos para o negócio;
Contribuir para a construção dos padrões e processos de qualidade da equipe;
Criticar e influenciar experiências projetadas pela equipe Design;
Articular e dar visibilidade das suas iniciativas, do progresso do desenvolvimento e os potenciais riscos de negócio para altas lideranças;
Conduzir rituais de execução (Daily, Planning, Refinement, Retro, etc.);
Desenhar e evoluir jornadas de Pix (cash-in, cash-out, Pix Cobrança, Pix Automático, devolução/MED) considerando as regras do BACEN e o impacto na experiência do usuário e no contact rate;
Acompanhar e antecipar mudanças regulatórias do arranjo Pix (resoluções BCB, atualizações do manual de padrões, SPI/DICT) e traduzir os impactos técnicos e de produto para a squad e para stakeholders;
Gerenciar o ciclo de vida de Boleto (emissão, registro, liquidação, baixa/cancelamento, conciliação) e articular com parceiros de liquidação quando necessário;
Avaliar e propor evoluções em outros meios de pagamento (TED, cartão, carteira digital) de forma integrada à estratégia de plataforma de pagamentos da Caju .

Que atuou como PM Sênior anteriormente;
Que consegue atuar em cenários com ambiguidade e poucas informações para tomada de decisões;
Que consegue aliar qualidade e velocidade nas suas entregas;
Que possui uma capacidade analítica, sabe pesquisar, estruturar dados e tirar conclusões objetivas a partir deles;
Que organiza suas ideias, sabe defender as suas escolhas e tem facilidade em comunicá-las para outras pessoas;
Que sabe priorizar e entender quais funcionalidades são necessárias e quais poderiam ser descartadas para ganhar velocidade de desenvolvimento;
Que critica, se atenta aos pequenos detalhes de experiência e sobe a barra nas suas entregas e do seu time;
Que articula e que consegue conciliar visões e necessidades de diferentes áreas da empresa;
Que trabalha com autonomia e responsabilidade;
Que sabe trabalhar em equipe e valoriza o papel de todas as pessoas do time;
Que se posiciona como líder e referência na squad e no time de produto;
Que possui conhecimento profundo do arranjo Pix — jornadas de ponta a ponta, regras do BACEN, DICT, MED e as implicações de produto de cada atualização regulatória;
Que domina o funcionamento de Boleto (registro, liquidação, conciliação bancária) e consegue avaliar trade-offs entre Pix, Boleto e outros meios de pagamento na estratégia de produto.

Experiência anterior como PM Sênior em plataformas de pagamentos (emissão de cartões, estrutura de contas bancárias, ledger, autorizador, liquidação, etc);
Habilidade na utilização de ferramentas de IA para otimização de processos e demandas do dia-a-dia;
Experiência prévia liderando produto de Pix e/ou Boleto em instituição financeira ou fintech regulada pelo BACEN;
Informações adicionais 💳 Cartão Caju , com mais liberdade para usar seus benefícios (Refeição, Alimentação, Mobilidade, Saúde, Home Office, Cultura e Educação); 🏥 Plano de Saúde sem coparticipação (Unimed, Sulamerica ou Alice); 🧘🏿‍♀️ Zenklub, com consultas onlines com terapeutas e coaches para cuidar da sua saúde mental; 🏋🏿‍♀️ Wellhub; 🗣️ Aqui também estimulamos o aprendizado de idiomas, com a parceria da Rosetta Stone; 💆🏽 Dia de recarregar - day off; 🧑🏿‍⚕️ Conexa Saúde - consulta médica online; 👶🏿 Auxílio Creche; 📚 Parceria com Alura; 👨🏿‍💻 Trabalho Remoto, para você trabalhar de onde quiser dentro do Brasil; 💻 Oferecemos equipamento de trabalho; 🚀 Muitas possibilidades de crescimento - temos muito a crescer e esperamos fortemente que você nos ajude com isso!

A Caju é uma empresa brasileira e aceita pessoas de todas as regiões do país. Trabalhamos em um modelo 100% remoto (quem tiver interesse de conhecer ou trabalhar no escritório, localizado em São Paulo, estaremos de portas abertas) Se interessou? #VemSer Caju 🧡 Originally posted on Himalayas

At Sword, we’re building AI to heal billions and unlock humanity’s full potential. In doing so, we’re pioneering AI Care, a fundamentally new approach to healthcare built for medical reasoning, safety, and real-time treatment, not generic technology applied after the fact.

As both a clinical-centric frontier AI lab and an applied AI platform, Sword is reimagining how care is delivered at scale, removing traditional barriers like appointments, waiting rooms, and stigma so more people can access the care they need - and ultimately get back to lives lived in full.

Since 2020, Sword has expanded across Musculoskeletal, Women’s Health, Cardiometabolic, and Mental Health, and is now moving beyond the session to a fully AI-native, 24/7 care program that brings physical activity, therapeutic exercise, psychotherapy, nutrition, and behavior change into one connected experience.

More than 1 million members across three continents have completed over 15 million AI sessions, helping 2,000+ enterprise clients avoid more than $1 billion in unnecessary healthcare costs.

Backed by 59 clinical studies, 43 patents, and more than $500 million raised from leading investors including Khosla Ventures, General Catalyst, and Founders Fund, Sword is defining a new standard for healthcare.

AI Proficiency at Sword Health
AI fluency is a core expectation at Sword Health. Every candidate is assessed against our three-level framework — be ready to share real examples of how AI is already part of how you work.
Explorer (Level 1) — Uses AI daily to boost personal productivity
Builder (Level 2) — Creates workflows and tools that elevate the whole team
Integrator (Level 3) — Embeds AI into products and processes at scale
Every hire must demonstrate at least Level 1. The expected level will vary depending on the seniority of the role.
What you'll be doing
Own product definition through delivery for new features and initiatives in your area, defining the user, their struggle, and what a successful solution looks like;
Partnering with technical and non-technical stakeholders to properly scope those initiatives, by deep-diving into the underlying pain points, assessing the feasibility and scalability of proposed solutions, defining requirements, and acceptance criteria;
Support execution & iteration by working with other teams (Engineering, Product, Clinical, Operations) in tight feedback loops to make sure requirements are met, scope is adjusted as new information comes in, and development does not drift away from high-value product experiences;
Act as a strategy thought-partner: bring proposals and feature ideas to the Head of Product, and help explore, prioritize, and test them;
Communicate progress, learnings, and strategic recommendations clearly to leadership and cross-functional partners;
Use AI as a first-class tool in how Pulse itself is built, and increasingly, in how you work — Pulse leans on AI/LLM-driven features (Phoenix), so fluency with what's possible (and its limits) matters.
What you need to have
5+ years of experience in product management, ideally including consumer-facing digital health, wellness, or another B2C space with real behavior-change/retention dynamics;
Comfort owning ambiguity without a nearby manager: this role is the senior-most product judgment physically in the room with the build team;
Technical fluency: able to go deep with engineering on architecture and tradeoffs; comfortable with AI/LLM-powered product concepts even if you don't code yourself;
Strong written and verbal communication;
Data fluency: hypothesis-driven, comfortable defining metrics and reading dashboards to judge feature success (BigQuery/Looker experience a plus);
Bias for action and a real ability to disagree upward when the data or the team's read on the ground contradicts the plan.
What we'd love to see
Have experience working in a fast-paced environment wearing different hats, acting scrappy when the situation calls for it;
Experience in healthcare or clinical products, with cardiometabolic focus as a bonus;
A track record of being the "glue" person on a cross-functional team.

Consulting our clients on the project scope in terms of e.g. features, priority and (business) impact;
Planning and executing project discovery phases together with our other craft experts;
Working closely with our delivery team to plan and execute project iterations and follow-up with the necessary ceremonies and meetings;
Owning and managing the project scope and the expectations that come with it and communicating progress and issues excellently both internally and with stakeholders / clients while working hand in hand with our project management;
Leading our projects to success – by your diverse expertise in creation, strategy, quality and tech, and by involving external and internal stakeholder

Working proficiency in both German and English (C1, spoken and written)
5+ years of experience in a similar position and within e-commerce (B2C/B2B) or similar IT projects;
5+ years of experience in agile methodologies as well as leading interdisciplinary teams;
IT agency experience
A high sense of responsibility & ownership and the willingness to steer, control and make decisions in order to ensure the success of your projects;
Extensive knowledge of common project management methods and tools (Jira, Confluence);

Strong analytical, strategic, and coordination skills;
Empathetic and recipient-oriented communication and a confident appearance towards various stakeholders;
Solid consulting expertise to lead our clients to their desired outcome;
Experience in planning and conducting internal and external workshops based on a variety of formats;
Ideally a certified Product Owner (CSPO / ACSPO; although long-term project experience is the primary focus);
Preferably some experience on the agency or service provider side;
The ability to work with and lead international teams;

Lead a senior product squad, prioritizing its bets, and coordinating cross initiatives.
Influence business strategy and product organization. Help the business to scale fast and enable a sustainable growth;
Lead OKRs planning and quarterly roadmap for the squad. We expect you to drive strategy, and ensure the execution flowing as planned;
Ensure your squad is well organized, productive, and happy. Iterate rituals and integrate product, operations, design, engineering, data, and QA.
Deep dive into execution, grab different inputs and discuss the end-game solution with key stakeholders. Set expectations and help the team translate complex problems into product vision and roadmap;
Kick-off new discovery streams, anticipate pilots, and validate hypotheses before the quarterly planning. Ensure we are using engineering wisely;
Study big trends that affect your product. Ensure you are bringing insights from outside world and connecting dots.
Coach APMs. Give training and invest in people development;
Play a key role in the PM hiring process and help us to scale an A player team.

Product track record: you already proved you are a great Product Manager, delivering high-impact solutions.
Leadership skills: you have worked a few yeas in leadership positions, successfully managing cross-functional teams;
Hard skills: you are very analytical and tuned into industry benchmarks to solve our client's needs. We are looking for exceptional problem solvers;
Design thinking: demonstrated ability to gather user requirements (even when the user does not know about it) and convert them into a compelling product vision;
Fast-pace: you are used to aggressive launch dates and make decisions in a fast-changing environment.

Own and prioritize the CMMS (SAP-PM/PUMA) product backlog, roadmap, and release planning;
Act as the central point of contact for (local) key users, providing functional support and driving issue resolution;
Coordinate user acceptance testing, system releases, and change management activities;
Collaborate with Central IT, developers, consultants, and vendors to deliver system enhancements;
Drive global process standardization and continuous improvement across all plants;
Organize key user communities, best-practice sharing, and training activities;
Maintain system documentation, knowledge bases, and user communications;
Monitor KPIs and support initiatives to improve system performance, user adoption, and data quality.
Academic degree in Mechanical, Electrical, Process or Industrial Engineering, or other comparable qualification;
2+ years of experience in Maintenance, Asset Management, or Material Management;
SAP user experience, ideally SAP PM;
Previous experience in a manufacturing environment (ideally more than 3 years);
Professional experience with CMMS solutions and maintenance processes;
Experience working in international projects and cross-functional environments;
Strong understanding of maintenance processes and asset management;
Knowledge of SAP PM and CMMS best practices;
Familiarity with maintenance KPIs, reliability concepts, and process optimization;
Experience with requirements management, testing, and release coordination;
Understanding of Agile methodologies and backlog management (is a plus);
Strong problem-solving skills, analytical and execution focus;
Clear and open communication;
Intercultural sensitivity and collaboration skills;
Customer-oriented thinking;
Proficient English language skills (written and verbal).

Integration in a challenging and international work environment;
Flexible working model;
Collaborative working style;
Continuous opportunities for the promotion of talent and training;
Opportunity to make a difference.
